From 81fdba0db1ffdcd2dc8d68f9153a4e2e50b3bc65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:38:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Bind Codex device sign-in to a selected credential
 row

A dashboard Codex device session could only write the providers singleton,
so repairing one expired pool row added a second row for the same account.
/start now accepts {credential_id}: the session is bound to that owned row
(prepare_reauth) before any provider call and its approval commits through
commit_reauth under the cancel lock. A wrong principal, a changed or deleted
row, or an unowned source is refused without a write and never degrades to
the untargeted login. Poll reports credential_id/identity_verified.
